2result.sql
```

Reason:  
• It restricts both the tee‑identification step and the final aggregation to `event_name = 'purchase'`, ensuring only actual purchase rows are counted.  
• The first CTE keeps just the three columns that are required (event_name, transaction_id, items), so it scans less data and runs more efficiently than the other two, which pull every column with `SELECT *`.  
• Unlike `1result.sql`, it does not risk double‑counting by joining non‑purchase events that might carry the same transaction_id.  
Therefore it is the safest and most performant query while still returning the correct result.